    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0378" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.506/37: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-18T15:00:00-03:00">October 18, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. My despatch No. 33 of September 14. My despatch No. 84 of Octobed 15<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d401-f1"/> reported the local representative of the American
                    Foreign Insurance Association optimistic as to the final outcome of the pending
                    insurance legislation due to presentation by a Deputy of a satisfactory
                    substitute bill. However, Cunningham now informs me the passage of the
                    objectionable legislation appears imminent due to the rejection of the
                    substitute bill and the approval of the original bill by the Finance Committee
                    of the Chamber of Deputies. This committee at the same time approved a motion
                    requesting information <pb facs="0379" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/> from the
                    Minister of Finance as to the effect of this legislation upon the finances and
                    exchange position of Brazil but the wording of the motion is such that the bill
                    may be brought to the floor of the Chamber of Deputies before the receipt of the
                    information solicited.</p>
                <p>Minister of Finance gave me to understand a few days ago he is opposed to the
                    bill but I understand it is being pushed by the Minister of Labor<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d401-f2"/> with the approval of the President and it is uncertain
                    whether the Minister of Finance will be able to effect a change favorable to the
                    insurance companies.</p>
                <p>I have called the attention of the Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d401-f3"/> to the Embassy’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of May 6 reported in the Embassy’s telegram No. 42, May
                    8, 10 a.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
